-## Band Selection
+**Minimum SNR:** Ignore spots weaker than this threshold. Range: -30 to 0 dB.
+
+---
+
+## DXpedition Chase
+
+The dedicated DXpedition section controls catalogue-driven chasing without
+weakening the normal safety boundaries. A network report must contain explicit
+FT8 mode evidence, its band must be enabled and inside its schedule, and MSHV
+must decode the station locally after QSY before it can call.
+
+| Setting | Default | Meaning |
+|---------|---------|---------|
+| Enable catalogue-driven chasing | On | Use active `dxpedition_watch.json` entries for priority and QSY handling |
+| Same-band off-standard QSY | On | Permit a verified expedition spot to move away from the standard FT8 dial on the current band |
+| Cross-band DXpedition QSY | On | Permit an idle engine to change to another open, enabled band for an expedition |
+| Chase scope | Needed only | `Any active` also permits an active catalogue call that has not yet been worked on that band |
+| Minimum independent spotters | 1 | Required network confidence before an expedition QSY |
+| Maximum spot age | 120 seconds | Maximum age of external evidence used for expedition QSY |
+| Local verification timeout | 60 seconds | Canonical cross-band/off-standard listen time before abandoning an unverified spot |
+| TX offset above expedition | 1000 Hz | Audio-frequency separation requested for a verified expedition call, clamped to the FT8 passband |
+| Priority boost | 12000 | Score added to an otherwise eligible catalogue entry |
+| Return to standard dial | On | Return after an off-standard completion or verification timeout |
+
+The read-only catalogue line shows validity, active callsign/band aliases, and
+expiry. A valid catalogue is authoritative for expedition membership. The
+small built-in rare-prefix table remains only as a conservative fallback for a
+new announcement or temporarily unavailable catalogue.
+
+`Any active` does not override Wavelog: a call already worked on that band is
+still rejected, and pending uploads remain an exact-once inhibition.
+
+---
+
+## Band Selection
 
 ### Enabled Bands
 
